      <h3><span style="margin-right: 0.4rem;">&#128221;</span> Quizzes</h3>
<p>Each of the thirteen units ends with a ten-question multiple-choice quiz that tests your understanding of the lesson and the works in it. These are <strong>self-study tools</strong>: you get instant feedback on every answer, so you can see what you have grasped and where to look again. Your answers are not recorded.</p>
<h4>What each quiz covers</h4>
<ul>
<li><strong>Quiz 1:</strong> The Humanities: An Introduction</li>
<li><strong>Quiz 2:</strong> What Is a Work of Art?</li>
<li><strong>Quiz 3:</strong> Being a Critic of the Arts</li>
<li><strong>Quiz 4:</strong> Painting</li>
<li><strong>Quiz 5:</strong> Sculpture</li>
<li><strong>Quiz 6:</strong> Architecture</li>
<li><strong>Quiz 7:</strong> Literature</li>
<li><strong>Quiz 8:</strong> Theater</li>
<li><strong>Quiz 9:</strong> Music</li>
<li><strong>Quiz 10:</strong> Dance</li>
<li><strong>Quiz 11:</strong> Photography</li>
<li><strong>Quiz 12:</strong> Cinema</li>
<li><strong>Quiz 13:</strong> Television and Video Art</li>
</ul>
<div class="callout callout--concept"><span class="callout__icon" aria-hidden="true">&#128161;</span><div class="callout__content">
<p><strong>Tip:</strong> Take each quiz after you have worked through the whole unit. Use Start Over as often as you like.</p>
</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

