  <div class="accordion__content">
    <div class="accordion__body">
      <h3><span style="margin-right: 0.4rem;">&#128172;</span> Reflection Prompts</h3>
<p>Each unit includes a reflection prompt: a question about a work, an art form, or an idea from the unit that asks you to form a reasoned response of your own. They take the place of traditional discussion boards.</p>
<h4>How to approach them</h4>
<ul>
<li>Read the prompt carefully and make sure you understand what is being asked</li>
<li>Look at or listen to the work again before you write</li>
<li>Support your response with specific details from the work, not just your general reaction</li>
<li>Aim for clarity over length; a focused paragraph or two is worth more than a rambling page</li>
</ul>
<div class="callout callout--note"><span class="callout__icon" aria-hidden="true">&#8505;&#65039;</span><div class="callout__content">
<p><strong>These are for your benefit.</strong> Your reflection is a space to practice thinking and writing about the arts. Nothing you type on the page is saved, so copy your work if you want to keep it.</p>
</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

